    "api_error_status": null,
    "result": "I fixed it in `hits.go`, but I could not run the tests because the `go test` command needs your approval.\n\nThe count was low because two processes can read the same count and both write back n+1, so one view is lost. Also, `os.WriteFile` empties the file before it writes. A process that reads during that moment gets 0 and resets the count.\n\n- **What I changed:** `Hit` now adds one byte to the end of `\u003cpage\u003e.hits` in append mode. The operating system does each append in one step, so no process overwrites another's. `Total` returns the size of that file in bytes.\n- **Old counts are kept:** `Total` also adds the number in any existing `\u003cpage\u003e.count` file. That file is now only read.\n- **New test:** `hits_test.go` starts 8 separate processes that make 200 hits each and checks that the total is 1600. It also checks that the old count is included.\n\nRun `go test ./...` to check it.\n\n**TLDR**\nViews were lost when two processes updated the count file at the same time. Each hit is now one byte appended to `\u003cpage\u003e.hits`, and `Total` returns the file size plus any old `.count` value.\nRun `go test ./...`. I could not run it without your approval.",
